From 870167fad062e74f6de27e76db84d17cc49d8b84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:56:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750-erhai: describe PCIe WAKE# as active
 low

WAKE# is an active-low signal, as the PCIe CEM specification defines it
and as the other SM8750 boards describe it. The property was unused
until the PCI core started requesting wake-gpios as a wakeup interrupt;
with the active-high flag the idle line counts as asserted, and every
s2idle entry is woken within about two seconds by the root port's wake
interrupt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 30ab14d7c24d9309129b5467ffb4b81242af22e9)

[opd2413: applied to arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
index b1c419b..634c6d8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-oneplus-pad2pro.dts
@@ -2228,7 +2228,7 @@
 };
 
 &pcieport0 {
-	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	wifi@0 {
